<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dionisio de Herrera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1781">1781</a>–<a href="/years/1850">1850</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dionisio de Herrera was a Honduran liberal lawyer and politician who became the first head of state of Honduras within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a>, serving from 1824 to 1827. He oversaw the state's first constitution of 1825, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comayagua">Comayagua</a> as capital, before conservatives backed by the federal president removed him. He later headed the government of Nicaragua from 1830 to 1833.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dionisio-de-herrera.jpg" alt="Dionisio de Herrera" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dionisio_de_Herrera.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
